.Dd September 24, 2026
.Dt LSBOM 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm lsbom
.Nd list the contents of a bill of materials (BOM) file
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl h
.Op Fl s
.Op Fl f | Fl d | Fl l | Fl b | Fl c
.Op Fl m
.Op Fl x
.Op Fl -arch Cm archVal
.Op Fl p Ar parameters
.Ar bomFile ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility reads one or more bill-of-materials files
.Ar bomFile
and prints their contents on standard output.
A BOM is a binary container used during installation to record the
files, directories, symbolic links, and other entries that a package
is expected to install.
.Pp
By default each entry is printed as:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
path	<octal mode>	owner/group	[	size	checksum	[ target ] ]
.Ed
.Pp
The size, checksum, and (for symbolic links) the target are printed
for entries other than directories; the target is the link target
stored in the BOM.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl h
Print full usage to standard error and exit.
.It Fl s
Print path names only.
.It Fl f , Fl d , Fl l , Fl b , Fl c
Print only files, directories, symbolic links, block devices, or
character devices respectively.
The flags select entries by their recorded path type and may be
combined; the default is to print entries of every type.
.It Fl m
Print the modified time of regular files, in ctime format, as an
additional trailing column.
.It Fl x
Suppress the mode for directories and symbolic links.
.It Fl -arch Ar archVal
Print metadata for the given architecture
.Pq Qq ppc , Qq i386 , Qq hppa , Qq sparc , Qq ppc64 , Qq x86_64 , Qq x86_64h , Qq arm64 , or Qq any .
For each Mach-O file the per-architecture values stored in the bom are used;
entries that do not contain the requested architecture are omitted.
.It Fl p Ar parameters
Print only the requested columns, in the order given.
Any of the following letters may be used, at most once:
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It f
file name
.It F
file name, quoted
.It m
file mode (octal)
.It M
symbolic file mode
.It g
group id
.It G
group name
.It u
user id
.It U
user name
.It t
modification time (seconds since the epoch)
.It T
formatted modification time
.It s
file size
.It S
formatted size
.It c
32-bit checksum
.It /
user id / group id
.It ?
user name / group name
.El
Fields are separated by tabs; fields that have no value are empty.
.El
.Pp
The output and diagnostics of this implementation are byte-for-byte
identical to those of Apple's lsbom for the BOM files this project
produces.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr mkbom 1 ,
.Xr bom 5
.Sh HISTORY
This implementation is a clean-room rewrite of the classic
.Nm
utility.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An LibreDarwin